Ever found yourself at a barn fire and there isn't a bucket nearby? You don't need a formula. Just follow these 4 steps. First, find the water hose or bucket (always a fire hose bucket!). Don't douse the whole barn. Start right at the edge. Second, lower hose until it hits the top of the fire. Third, keep moving. Keep moving until the water covers the fire. Fourth, keep your eyes on the hose. Spread fire to the other side. And if you see smoke coming from above, don't panic—just lower the hose.

Firefighters call this "holding the line." It's not about who says it first. It's about making sure the water hits the fire while you're moving. If you see flames near someone else, shout out "Fire!" and get them to move. Don't try to fight it alone. If you're unsure how to handle a small flare-up, call 911 for professional help before water gets wet.
